  },
  {
   "id": "done23",
   "type": "text",
   "x": -210,
   "y": 955,
   "width": 420,
   "height": 76,
   "text": "**block done?**    \nno masks left and unchanged, or the post-fill budget is spent",
   "color": "#64748b"
  },
  {
   "id": "commit24",
   "type": "text",
   "x": -210,
   "y": 1071,
   "width": 420,
   "height": 76,
   "text": "**yes → commit** the block, append the next 32 masks    \n(stop at `<|endoftext|>`)",
   "color": "2"
  },
  {
   "id": "loop-r1",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 1250,
   "y": 963,
   "width": 260,
   "height": 60,
   "text": "**no → next step**    \nwhole forward again",
   "color": "#f59e0b"
  },
  {
   "id": "loop-r2",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 1250,
   "y": -1550,
   "width": 260,
   "height": 60,
   "text": "↻ **denoising step**    \nwrites into the active block",
   "color": "#f59e0b"
  },
  {
   "id": "loop-l1",
   "type": "text",
   "x": -1520,
   "y": 1079,
   "width": 260,
   "height": 60,
   "text": "**next block**    \nactive → finished",
   "color": "2"
  },
  {
   "id": "loop-l2",
   "type": "text",
   "x": -1520,
   "y": -1550,
   "width": 260,
   "height": 60,
   "text": "**block committed**",
   "color": "2"
  },
  {
   "id": "note-ar",
   "type": "text",
   "x": -1180,
   "y": 518,
   "width": 640,
   "height": 230,
   "text": "**vs. autoregressive decoding**  \n- AR: causal mask, 1 forward → 1 new token at the right end, never revised.\n- Here: 1 forward predicts all 32 slots of the block at once; only confident ones are written, so a block of 32 needs between 1 and ~32 forwards (+ up to 16 refinement steps), and written tokens can still be rewritten (T2T), deleted or split.\n- This HF code keeps no KV cache: every step re-runs the full prefix."
  },
  {
   "id": "note-sample",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 560,
   "y": 648,
   "width": 600,
   "height": 120,
   "text": "Defaults (`generate()`): temperature 0 → x̂ = argmax; with temperature > 0, M2T samples (top-k / top-p) but p is still read from the unfiltered softmax. `<|mask|>` = id 156895, DELETE / INSERT = reserved ids 156930 / 156931. Anti-loop resampling if a block state repeats."
  }
 ],
